---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site-config';
import { SITES } from '../lib/sites';
import { breadcrumbJsonLd } from '../lib/seo';

const canonical = `${SITES.main}/manufacturing/`;
const jsonLd = [
  breadcrumbJsonLd([
    { name: 'Home', url: `${SITES.main}/` },
    { name: 'Manufacturing', url: canonical },
  ]),
];
---

<BaseLayout
  site={site}
  title="Charcoal Manufacturing & Sourcing"
  description="How we approach charcoal manufacturing and sourcing — multi-supplier qualification, standardized specifications and batch quality control."
  canonical={canonical}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: 'Home', url: '/' }, { name: 'Manufacturing', url: '/manufacturing/' }]}
>
  <div class="page-title container">
    <h1>Manufacturing &amp; Sourcing</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A China-based sourcing and supplier network — focused on transparency, standardization and
      sourcing efficiency rather than "China = cheap".
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>How We Source</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-2">
        <div class="card"><h3>Multi-supplier qualification</h3><p>We qualify multiple manufacturers so buyers can compare specifications.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Standardized specifications</h3><p>One spec model across all products — ash, moisture, fixed carbon, size, burn time.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Batch quality control</h3><p>Testing per batch with results labeled by source.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><h3>Export readiness</h3><p>Documentation and container loading for international shipping.</p></div>
      </div>

      <h2>The Coconut Shell Charcoal Process Chain</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          The following is the general process chain for coconut shell charcoal briquettes, drawn
          from public industry descriptions. It is shared manufacturing knowledge, not a claim
          about any specific factory's equipment or output.
        </p>
        <ol>
          <li><strong>Carbonization</strong> — coconut shells are heated with limited oxygen to drive off volatiles and leave carbon.</li>
          <li><strong>Crushing</strong> — the carbonized shell is ground to a controlled particle size.</li>
          <li><strong>Mixing</strong> — the carbon powder is blended, typically with a binder, to a uniform paste.</li>
          <li><strong>Forming</strong> — the paste is pressed into shape (cube or flat briquettes).</li>
          <li><strong>Cutting</strong> — pressed stock is cut to the nominal size (e.g. 25 mm).</li>
          <li><strong>Drying</strong> — briquettes are dried to a low, controlled moisture content.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>
          Each step is a point where the final specification can drift: under-carbonization raises
          volatile matter, inconsistent crushing changes density and burn rate, and incomplete
          drying raises moisture. That is why batch testing matters — the process chain only
          produces a predictable product when each stage is controlled.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2>Why Standardized Specifications Matter</h2>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>
          A manufacturing claim is only useful when it is measurable. We use one specification
          model — ash, moisture, fixed carbon, volatile matter, size tolerance and burning time —
          across all products, so a buyer can compare suppliers on the same axes. The definitions
          live on the
          <a href={`${SITES.data}/specifications/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">data sub-site</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="callout-pending">
        <span class="callout-title">Data pending — supplier verification in progress</span>
        <p>
          Manufacturer profiles, production capacities and certifications are published only after
          supplier verification. See the manufacturer sub-site for the qualification model.
        </p>
        <p><a href={`${SITES.manufacturer}/`} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Manufacturer Intelligence →</a></p>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-banner">
        <h2>Need manufacturing capacity?</h2>
        <p>Tell us your product and volume.</p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/request-quote/">Request a Quote →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
